[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mBrowser app only (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mInstrument app.js — the login form, validation, and API call. Requires deciding how logs escape the user's browser
[39m     [38;5;246mto reach you.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Node entry point only
     [38;5;246mInstrument src/index.js and src/utils.js. Cheap (stdout/file) but there is little real behavior there to debug.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both, shared logger
     [38;5;246mOne logger module with a browser backend and a Node backend. Most design work; one vocabulary across both.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Both, separate loggers
     [38;5;246mTwo small independent loggers. Less upfront design, but conventions drift over time.[39m
